From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 08:41:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 115/115] The automation view regains focus without a parameter
 its Clip's new type lacks: no E411 after CV in the instrument browser

A synth Clip's automation view with a patched parameter selected opens the
synth browser with LOAD + SYNTH; CV (or MIDI) there changes the Clip's type
and closes the browser. AutomationView::focusRegained() then rendered the
old parameter through InstrumentClipMinder::focusRegained() and the knob
levels, which looked it up in the CV Clip's params: E411 in
ModelStackWithThreeMainThings::getPatchedAutoParamFromId() (the fuzzer's
seed 202, stop run 8). The view resets such a selection when it opens and
before session or arranger view pre-render it, not when it regains focus.
For an instrument Clip whose type changed, focusRegained() now forgets the
selected parameter before InstrumentClipMinder::focusRegained() sets the
view's model stack to the new Output and renders, and resets the rest of
the selection after it. The whole reset can't come first: it refreshes the
knob levels while the model stack still has the old synth (E411 in
Sound::getParamFromModEncoder()).

The view also notes the Clip's type when a parameter is selected (a pad or
the select encoder), not only when it opens: in the seed the view's own
SYNTH had made a CV clip a synth, LPF resonance was selected, and the type
noted was still CV, so CV in the browser looked like no change.

Test (beta-1.3/tests/repro/automation_browser_type_emu.py): LPF frequency
selected, LOAD + SYNTH, CV: back in the automation view with no parameter
selected (before: E411); the browser left with BACK keeps the selection;
a CV clip made a synth by the view's SYNTH, LPF frequency, LOAD + SYNTH, CV:
no parameter selected (before: E411).
---
 src/deluge/gui/views/automation_view.cpp | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/deluge/gui/views/automation_view.cpp b/src/deluge/gui/views/automation_view.cpp
index 9bc3e69f..50851b1a 100644
--- a/src/deluge/gui/views/automation_view.cpp
+++ b/src/deluge/gui/views/automation_view.cpp
@@ -487,6 +487,17 @@ void AutomationView::focusRegained() {
 			view.setActiveModControllableTimelineCounter(clip);
 		}
 		else {
+			// The Clip's type can change while a UI is open on top of this view (CV or MIDI in the instrument browser).
+			// The view's model stack keeps the old Output until InstrumentClipMinder::focusRegained() below sets the new
+			// one and renders the selected parameter: forget a parameter the new type may not have before that (a
+			// patched one froze with E411 in a CV clip), and reset the rest of the selection after it
+			bool outputTypeChanged = clip->output->type != clip->lastSelectedOutputType;
+			bool resetSelection = outputTypeChanged && inAutomationEditor();
+			if (resetSelection) {
+				clip->lastSelectedParamID = params::kNoParamID;
+				clip->lastSelectedParamKind = params::Kind::NONE;
+			}
+
 			// check if patch cable previously selected is still valid
 			// if not we'll reset parameter selection and go back to overview
 			if (clip->lastSelectedParamKind == params::Kind::PATCH_CABLE) {
@@ -511,6 +522,13 @@ void AutomationView::focusRegained() {
 			instrumentClipView.auditioningSilently = false; // Necessary?
 			InstrumentClipMinder::focusRegained();
 			instrumentClipView.setLedStates();
+
+			if (resetSelection) {
+				initParameterSelection(false);
+			}
+			if (outputTypeChanged) {
+				clip->lastSelectedOutputType = clip->output->type;
+			}
 		}
 	}
 
@@ -1991,6 +2009,7 @@ void AutomationView::handleParameterSelection(Clip* clip, Output* output, Output
 	else {
 		clip->lastSelectedParamShortcutX = xDisplay;
 		clip->lastSelectedParamShortcutY = yDisplay;
+		clip->lastSelectedOutputType = outputType; // The type the parameter was selected for
 	}
 
 	resetParameterShortcutBlinking();
@@ -2662,6 +2681,10 @@ void AutomationView::selectEncoderAction(int8_t offset) {
 		return;
 	}
 
+	if (!onArrangerView) {
+		clip->lastSelectedOutputType = outputType; // The type the parameter was selected for
+	}
+
 	// update name on display, the LED mod indicators, and refresh the grid
 	lastPadSelectedKnobPos = kNoSelection;
 	if (multiPadPressSelected && padSelectionOn) {
